      "role": "user",
      "content": "I guess so, but it feels like you're still treating \"reducing inequality\" as the ultimate goal that we have to work around the economy for. If the data shows that wealth taxes generally lead to less investment and slower growth, shouldn't we just conclude they aren't actually \"effective\" tools in a real-world setting?",
